  "etymologyNotes": [
    {
      "s": "makemeahanzi",
      "t": "A person bent over with long hair 匕 and a crutch; compare 耂"
    },
    {
      "s": "dong_chinese",
      "t": "Pictograph of an old person with long hair bent over and leaning on a cane."
    },
    {
      "s": "shuowen_jiezi",
      "t": "考也。七十曰老。从人、毛、匕。言須髮變白也。凡老之屬皆从老。",
      "w": 1
    },
    {
      "s": "wiktionary",
      "t": "Ideogrammic compound (會意 /会意): 人 (“man”) + 毛 (“hair”) + 匕 (“cane”) – a man with long hair (an old man), leaning on a cane. Compare top component to 孝 (OC *qʰruːs).\nCognate to 考 (OC *kʰluːʔ); the most commonly cited example of 轉注 (“reciprocal meaning”).\nUnknown. Compare Proto-Sino-Tibetan *s-raw (“withered, residue, corpse”), *rwat (“stiff, tough”), whence Burmese ရော် (rau, “wither, become overripe; age”), ရွတ် (rwat, “old, stiff, tough”). See also 古 (gǔ), 故 (gù).\nAn old Sino-Vietnamese borrowing is rệu (“overripe, pulpy”)."
    }
  ],
  "shuowen": "考也。七十曰老。从人、毛、匕。言須髮變白也。凡老之屬皆从老。",
